    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "One of the most retold myths in Egypt was the story of Osiris and his
    wife Isis. After Osiris was killed by the evil god Seth, Isis traveled through
    Egypt finding the separated parts of his body and putting them back together.
    \n\nShe revived him, wrapped in a mummies garments, and made Osiris the ruler
    of the underworld. Isis then gave birth to their son Horus, who would become
    one of the most important gods in ancient Egyptian lore. Isis is often depicted
    with wings, and Osiris can be distinguished by his Bluish-green skin. \n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 756a8c9b083f04819b8b1c63c736172c, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -633874113913258559, guid: 756a8c9b083f04819b8b1c63c736172c,
