  m_text: "The first cities of Egypt were small and dirty by modern standards. They
    were mainly just mud houses packed together.\n\nWhat helped hold these ancient
    communities together were shared beliefs in gods. \n\nOver the 7,000 years of
    ancient Egyptian society, over 2,000 gods were worshipped, each god having their
    own set of temples and cult followings. "
