  m_text: "The Egyptians are famous for their religious beliefs surrounding death.
    They mummified all of their dead, believing this was the way for the soul to
    reach the afterlife. \n\nThis process involved removing the organs of the deceased,
    treating the body with chemicals, then wrapping it in strips of linen before
    burial. "
