  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Like most ancient peoples, the Egyptians were very religious. Much of
    what we know about their culture is contained in their myths: stories they told
    to each other that explained the natural world.


    The Egyptians believed
    that every day the sun god Ra would carry the sun across the sky. When it became
    night, he would take the sun and would travel across the lakes beyond the sky,
    sometimes accompanied by other gods while being attacked by all the evils of
    the Underworld. He would still return every morning to make the journey across
    the sky.


'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 756a8c9b083f04819b8b1c63c736172c, type: 2}
