  m_text: "Part of the success of the Egyptian society was the invention of writing.
    They pressed papyrus reeds into sheets and wrote on them with ink made from organic
    materials. \n\nTheir language consisted of pictures called \u2018Hieroglyphs\u2019,
    which could be combined with their number system to record transactions as well
    as stories. \n"
